{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposal fails to provide sufficient information to enable an accurate assessment of the application. In particular, there is inconsistent and deficient information pertaining to the existing and proposed use, design and operation of the site. Based on the site visits, conflict between the information provided and the current situation on site was also observed. Given these reasons, officers are unable to determine the impact on neighbours, with particular concern surrounding noise and disturbance. As such, the proposal prejudices third parties who may otherwise have wished to comment on this application, and it cannot be accurately demonstrated that the proposal would be supported by the development plan. As such, the proposal is at odds with the following policies which seek a high quality design with acceptable neighbouring impacts:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- The&amp;nbsp;National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, 2023);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- Policies D4, D8, D13, D14 and SI1 of the London Plan (2021);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policy CP3 of the LBBD&#x27;s&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies BE2, BP8 and BP11 of the LBBD&#x27;s Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (2011);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp;Policies DMD1, DMD6, and DMSI3 of the LBBD&#x27;s&amp;nbsp;Draft Local Plan (Regulation 19 Submission Version, 2021).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
